body:
### bug

In this example:

```
chapter "The Raven"
author "Edgar Allan Poe"
section "First Act" {
  paragraph {
    "Once upon a midnight dreary, while I pondered, weak and weary,"
    "Over many a quaint and " bold{"curious"} " volume of forgotten lore-\"
  }
  paragraph {
    "While I nodded, nearly napping, suddenly there came a tapping,"
    "As of some one " italic{"gently"} " rapping-rapping at my chamber door."
  }
}
```

As written, `bold{"curious"}` is an argument in the directive starting `"Over many a quaint and "`, so it can't have subdirectives.

These need to be on separate lines:

```
chapter "The Raven"
author "Edgar Allan Poe"
section "First Act" {
  paragraph {
    "Once upon a midnight dreary, while I pondered, weak and weary,"
    "Over many a quaint and "
    bold{"curious"}
    " volume of forgotten lore-\"
  }
  paragraph {
    "While I nodded, nearly napping, suddenly there came a tapping,"
    "As of some one "
    italic{"gently"}
    " rapping-rapping at my chamber door."
  }
}
```

Now bold and italic are their own directives so they can have subdirectives.
